      "settingGeometryVersion": "1.2.0",
      "description": "A solid collar built by offsetting the stone's own girdle outline — the bezel's verified offset pipeline, reused rather than reimplemented — extruded from the attachment plane to a rim above the girdle, with the stone's own solid then cut out of it. The cut is the existing REFERENCE_SEAT relief, so the stone is a cutting tool and never becomes production metal. Relief is a PRECONDITION of this family rather than an option: without it the collar buries the stone, so the generator refuses and JM-SETTING-010 reports it. The rim height must stay below the stone's measured crown height, which is a geometric precondition and not a setting depth."
    },
